2. If meat be spoilt, and a good quantity of dairy food, or a milking, or a brewing [is at risk], hallow the medicinal herbs [worts], place them into and under the vat, and under the door; use lupins, and clifwort, and betony, and bishopwort.

Section LXVIII.
In the event that a hunting spider (that is, the stronger kind of spider) bites a man: make three scarifications [small incisions] close to the bite and directed away from it; let the blood run into a fresh green hazel-wood spoon, then throw it away over the road; then no harm will come of it. Again, make a scarification on the wound; pound leechwort [a medicinal herb]; lay it on; no harm will befall the man. Against the bite of a weaving spider: take the lower portion of seferthe [unidentified plant], and lichen from the blackthorn;

